</section>

<!-- Key Innovations -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="section-label">04 — Key Innovations</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">What makes this different.</h2>

  <div class="innovation-grid">
    <div class="innovation-card">
      <div class="tag">Identity</div>
      <h3>QR as Vehicle Passport</h3>
      <p>Users generate a permanent QR code at park.nl — no app, no account, no download. Add it to Apple Wallet or screenshot it. One generation, infinite uses across every meter in the country.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="innovation-card">
      <div class="tag">Time</div>
      <h3>Preset Time Blocks + Pay-as-You-Go</h3>
      <p>Six large tap targets for common durations replace the scroll-wheel picker. Unsure how long? Check in with €0.00 and check out when you return — pay only for actual time used.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="innovation-card">
      <div class="tag">Payment</div>
      <h3>Top-Mounted NFC with Ambient Feedback</h3>
      <p>Payment zone at natural hand height with a glowing ring: blue = ready, pulsing green = processing, solid green = success, red flash = retry. No ambiguity about what just happened.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="innovation-card">
      <div class="tag">Resilience</div>
      <h3>Graceful Degradation at Every Step</h3>
      <p>QR fails → manual keyboard. NFC fails → physical card slot. Internet down → offline mode with local validation. No single point of failure can block a payment.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="innovation-card full-width">
      <div class="tag">Intelligence</div>
      <h3>Contextual Awareness</h3>
      <p>The meter knows its zone and current pricing. It shows "valid until" time immediately. On the success screen, it offers "Extend Parking" for the inevitable "one more coffee" moment. After hours, it tells you parking is free. It's not just a payment terminal — it understands the context of why you're standing in front of it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Environmental Design -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="section-label">05 — Environmental Design</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">Designed for the real world, not a Figma artboard.</h2>
  <p class="section-desc">A parking meter in Amsterdam faces rain, frost, direct sunlight, and drunk tourists. The design must survive all of them.</p>

  <div class="env-grid">
    <div class="env-card">
      <div class="icon">☀️</div>
      <h4>Sunlight Readability</h4>
      <p>High-contrast dark UI with 1000+ nit transflective display. Green-on-dark palette chosen specifically for outdoor visibility — green has highest luminous efficiency for human vision.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="env-card">
      <div class="icon">🌧️</div>
      <h4>Rain & Wet Hands</h4>
      <p>Projected capacitive touch with rain-rejection algorithm. Large 48px minimum touch targets tolerate imprecise wet-finger taps. Physical card slot as fallback.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="env-card">
      <div class="icon">🧤</div>
      <h4>Glove Compatibility</h4>
      <p>Screen sensitivity tuned for up to 3mm glove thickness. All interactive elements are minimum 56px — comfortably tappable even with winter gloves.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="env-card">
      <div class="icon">❄️</div>
      <h4>Cold Weather</h4>
      <p>Heated touchscreen prevents frost buildup. QR scanner uses infrared, unaffected by temperature. The "QR + NFC" flow requires zero screen touches in freezing conditions.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="env-card">
      <div class="icon">🔆</div>
      <h4>Night Visibility</h4>
      <p>Auto-dimming display prevents glare at night. QR scanner LED illuminates automatically. NFC zone ambient ring provides wayfinding in darkness.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="env-card">
      <div class="icon">🛡️</div>
      <h4>Vandal Resistance</h4>
      <p>Gorilla Glass display, recessed scanner, flush NFC zone. No protruding elements to damage. IP67 rated enclosure for full weather sealing.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Accessibility -->
<section class="section" id="accessibility">
  <div class="section-label">06 — Accessibility</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">Usable by everyone means designed for everyone.</h2>
  <p class="section-desc">True accessibility isn't a checklist — it's a design philosophy that makes the product better for all users.</p>

  <div class="a11y-features">
    <div class="a11y-card">
      <div class="a11y-icon">🔊</div>
      <div>
        <h4>Audio Feedback</h4>
        <p>Every screen transition and action triggers a distinct audio cue. Successful payment plays a pleasant confirmation tone. Error states use a gentle, non-alarming alert sound. Volume auto-adjusts to ambient noise levels.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="a11y-card">
      <div class="a11y-icon">📐</div>
      <div>
        <h4>Adjustable Screen Angle</h4>
        <p>The screen tilts 15° on a motorized mount, activated by a physical button at wheelchair height. Provides optimal viewing angle for both standing and seated users.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="a11y-card">
      <div class="a11y-icon">🎯</div>
      <div>
        <h4>Large Touch Targets</h4>
        <p>All interactive elements are minimum 48x48px (WCAG) with 56px preferred. High-contrast borders on all buttons. No gesture-dependent interactions — everything is a single tap.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="a11y-card">
      <div class="a11y-icon">🌍</div>
      <div>
        <h4>Multi-Language + Icons</h4>
        <p>4 languages with auto-detect based on card origin. Universal icons paired with text — the flow is understandable even without reading. Icon-only mode for maximum clarity.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="a11y-card">
      <div class="a11y-icon">🎨</div>
      <div>
        <h4>WCAG AAA Contrast</h4>
        <p>Green (#00e676) on dark (#111) exceeds 7:1 contrast ratio. No color-only indicators — all states use shape + color + animation. Tested for deuteranopia, protanopia, and tritanopia.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="a11y-card">
      <div class="a11y-icon">✋</div>
      <div>
        <h4>Physical Fallbacks</h4>
        <p>Hardware card slot below screen for chip+PIN payments. Tactile raised edge around NFC zone for positioning by touch. Braille label on physical interaction points.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Journey Comparison -->
<section class="section" id="comparison">
  <div class="section-label">07 — Journey Comparison</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">Side-by-side: old vs. new.</h2>

  <div class="comparison" style="margin-top: 40px;">
    <div class="journey-header">
      <span>Stage</span>
      <span>Old System</span>
      <span>Redesign</span>
    </div>
    <div class="journey-row">
      <div class="journey-stage">Approach</div>
      <div class="journey-old">Search for instructions. Try to understand cluttered interface with 5+ zones. Find the keyboard.</div>
      <div class="journey-new">Screen shows zone, price, and two clear options: Scan QR or Enter Plate. Language auto-detected.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="journey-row">
      <div class="journey-stage">Identify</div>
      <div class="journey-old">Hunt-and-peck license plate on ABC keyboard. Small buttons. Frequent errors. ~25 seconds.</div>
      <div class="journey-new">2-second QR scan or large-button keypad with auto-formatting and format validation. ~3-10 seconds.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="journey-row">
      <div class="journey-stage">Duration</div>
      <div class="journey-old">Scroll through a time wheel. Unclear pricing per increment. Hope you guessed right.</div>
      <div class="journey-new">Tap one of 6 preset buttons showing price. Or choose pay-as-you-go to avoid guessing entirely.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="journey-row">
      <div class="journey-stage">Payment</div>
      <div class="journey-old">Find card slot. Insert card. Wait. Unclear if it worked. Text-only confirmation in Dutch.</div>
      <div class="journey-new">Tap NFC at top of device. Ambient light ring confirms instantly: green = done. Takes 1-2 seconds.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="journey-row">
      <div class="journey-stage">Confirmation</div>
      <div class="journey-old">Small text says "Betaling geslaagd." No receipt. Anxiety about whether it actually worked.</div>
      <div class="journey-new">Full-screen success with checkmark, expiry time, reference number, and option to extend later.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="journey-row">
      <div class="journey-stage">Error</div>
      <div class="journey-old">Cryptic error code. Start over from scratch. No guidance on what went wrong.</div>
      <div class="journey-new">Plain-language explanation, specific fix suggestion, and always a fallback path to complete payment.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="journey-row">
      <div class="journey-stage">Total Time</div>
      <div class="journey-old" style="font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace; color: var(--error); font-weight: 700;">45–60 seconds</div>
      <div class="journey-new" style="font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700;">8 seconds (QR) · 25 seconds (manual)</div>
    </div>
  </div>

